B_n counts the partitions of an n-element set
(unlabeled nonempty disjoint subsets covering the whole set)

VARIABLES / TYPES
n     : cardinality of the ground set
B_n   : nth Bell number (integer)
k     : summation index (nonnegative integer)
partition : unordered collection of nonempty unlabeled blocks

FUNDAMENTALS
Dobinski formula
B_n = (1/e) * sum_{k=0}^∞ (k^n / k!)

Sequence
B_0 = 1
B_1 = 1
B_2 = 2
B_3 = 5
B_4 = 15
B_5 = 52

POST CLAIM
5 people form unlabeled teams in exactly 52 ways  →  B_5 = 52

USES
unlabeled clusters in machine learning
possible communities
every unlabeled bundling of data
set partitions decide groupings before any algorithm runs
